WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.270
I was told.

2
00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.610
She was asked.

3
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:03.960
We were given.

4
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.070
English loves this pattern.

5
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:08.180
French has the verb: «dire»,

6
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.140
to tell. But copy I
was told word for word,

7
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.980
and you get a sentence
French won't accept.

8
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:15.970
It isn't slang.

9
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.140
It isn't rude.

10
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.940
It just isn't French.

11
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.480
So why does French refuse a
sentence English finds so easy?

12
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.330
In this mission, you'll
split one English word,

13
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.100
was, into two French meanings.

14
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.720
Then you'll build long
verb chains in the lab,

15
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.580
ending by ending.

16
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.040
Your mission: explain why
French turns down a sentence

17
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.160
that English finds so easy.
